After every code update, bug fix, feature addition, or problem resolution, please update the @README.md file tohe current state of the project. This file should always serve as a clear, living guide to:

What we’re building

Why we’re building it

How each part of the codebase contributes to the whole

The current architecture, decisions made, and any tradeoffs


The goal is to make the README a reliable source of truth for anyone working on the project—whether it's you (Cursor), another dev, or even future me. As the codebase grows past 2,000+ lines and more people contribute, this documentation will be critical for keeping things understandable and maintainable.